                <pb facs="0331" n="266" xml:id="pg266"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.84/69: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Addis Ababa</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cramp</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis
                                Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-05T18:00:00+03:00">May 5, 1936—6 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        May 5—2:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>289. Entire Legation white personnel evacuated by British convoy this morning at
                    9:30. Italians arrived 4 p.m. I reoccupied the Legation with Tanner, Anslow and
                    Cavannah at 5 p.m. Everything untouched. The Minister and rest of personnel
                    remaining at British Legation until tomorrow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cramp</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
